+## Successor05: saved binary and documentation output classification
+
+The first actual read-only discovery04 exited 1 before creating a proposal or
+B3. Its full raw failure is retained. The complete saved 26-command compiler
+history contains 47 build-script compilations with no extra-filename flag and
+two rustdoc --test invocations; the original parser rejected these ordinary
+non-private-output forms. All 82 passed controls and source04 remain unchanged.
+
+Successor05 retains every command and adds only two explicit classifications.
+A build_script_build compiler command with exactly bin, dep-info+link, no test,
+no filename suffix and no output redirection emits no private library. Other
+missing-suffix library or mixed/metadata roles still fail. The exact bootstrap
+rustdoc shim permits only the observed rustc_interface/run_make_support
+--test source/target/cwd routes, rejecting persistent or redirected output.
+Bound rustc_session output.rs separates executable/library output names; bound
+rustdoc shim and doctest.rs use the temporary doctest output directory and
+rust_out executable when persistent output is absent. These are not compiler
+producer substitutions or claims about arbitrary build-script side effects.
+
+Eleven additional source controls include all 47+2 saved raw commands and negative
+role/redirect/response-file/mixed-output cases, plus the complete saved actual
+catalog against all256 stamped private producers. They are written but unrun.
+The complete competing-output history, latest private producer, two-shim route,
+full effective environment, actual stamp and provider guards remain required.
